  "fileVersion": "1.0",
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Focus-sized documents in the workspace",
    "description": "A graph is a combined document: Views, nodes and relationships render together as authored. Paid workspace focus expands one graph to its document size inside its own boundary; the previous graph contracts and neighboring graphs settle around the changed frames. Free mode has no surrounding workspace: the focused graph is the entire environment. This task supersedes fixed-frame-on-focus behavior, not the protection against repeated-click or zoom-driven reflow.",
