      "data": {
        "rationale": "This keeps the conversation anchored to a real graph artifact instead of a floating abstraction.",
        "status": "accepted",
        "decidedAt": "",
        "owner": "",
        "supersededBy": "",
        "body": "Detail is focused consumption of the combined graph, not a page-only substitute or a numeric resolution rung. Summary is the largest represented View, Icon the smallest; intermediate representations are allowed, then Glyph and Dot fallbacks. Paid graph document size is in workspace coordinates, not fullscreen. Only a focus transition changes compact/document frame mode. Repeated focused clicks and ordinary zoom do not resize or reflow. Keep camera zoom fixed; pan may bring a newly focused graph into view. Expansion must stay clipped to graph bounds, keep public handles accessible, and preserve manual sizes. Animate frame and neighbor movement together; reduced motion applies.",
