      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "Define frame ownership and defaults",
        "body": "Separate authored document bounds, compact workspace frame, transient presentation geometry and camera state. Use the current Declaration/landing-surface/membrane contracts; do not store automatic layout in node positions. Resolve Q1 and Q2 before choosing new persistent fields. Inspect graphWorkspace.js, workspaceCamera.js and graphViewPresentation.js.\n\nStarted 2026-09-25. Reviewed against the current code: graphRenderBounds() (authored bounds), instance.frame/resizeGraphMembrane() (manual size), and _workspacePresentationFrame (transient) already exist as separate things in graphWorkspace.js — this task is mostly naming and precedence, not new plumbing. The real blocker for Tasks 2-4 is workspaceCamera.js layoutWorkspaceInstances(), which currently keeps focus from resizing anything on purpose.\n\nBuilt (2026-09-25): authoredDocumentBounds(), defaultCompactFrame(), resolveCompactFrame() and setCompactFrame() in graphWorkspace.js, with a frame-ownership contract comment naming and ordering all four concepts (authored document bounds, compact workspace frame, transient presentation geometry, camera). The compact frame persists on instance.frame with mode \"workspace\" (previously an unused stub value the parser already recognized), separate from the authored mode \"authored\" resizeGraphMembrane() writes. setCompactFrame() never touches the graph itself, so it carries no document authority, matching resizeGraphMembrane()'s does. Default compact size reuses the existing LEVEL_BOX_SIZE.summary constant rather than inventing a new one. 5 new tests in graphWorkspace.test.js (60/60 passing); full suite 1078/1078. Deliberately NOT wired into regionBounds()/rendering yet -- every instance still occupies its authored size regardless of focus at runtime. Wiring focus-dependence into layoutWorkspaceInstances and the placement helpers is task 3's job, not this one.",
        "priority": "high",
        "status": "done",
        "owner": "",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "Document size precedence and compact-frame policy are explicit",
          "Legacy graphs have deterministic fallbacks; manual resize remains authoritative"
        ],
        "definitionKey": "task",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "task",
          "sourceRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node",
