      "data": {
        "title": "Implement a single focus transition",
        "body": "In useGraphWorkspace.js, unify click, explicit focus, link/Portal navigation, open, reload and #nodeId entry. Expand the new focus and contract the old focus in one update. Preserve editing-session versus focused-graph identity.\n\nBuilt (2026-09-25): activateInstance() in useGraphWorkspace.js was already the real funnel most callers (click, the header's Focus button, Portal/link navigation via focusLoadedInstance, #nodeId entry) go through -- the earlier \"9 files\" count was mostly consumers of that one API, not 9 independent implementations. Two concrete violations of this task's own acceptance criteria were found by reading the code and fixed: (1) right-click on a workspace instance (WorkspaceLayer.js) called workspace.activateInstance() before opening its context menu, swapping the editing session merely to show a menu -- removed; the menu still receives { scope: \"graph\", instanceId }, so explicit focus from within it stays possible. (2) focusAtScreenPoint()'s miss branch (clicking empty canvas) only cleared focusedGraphInstanceId, leaving a stale focused node/fragment and, if the camera had rolled over into a graph-local scope, no way back to workspace scope -- it now calls the one focusWorkspace() defocus path instead of a second, partial reset. 2 new regression tests in graphWorkspace.test.js (62/62); full suite 1080/1080. Editing-session (activeGraphInstanceId) versus focused-graph (focusedGraphInstanceId) identity was already distinct (selectNodeInInstance can set the former without the latter) and is unchanged. Frame expansion/contraction on focus is still task 3's job -- this task was about the transition mechanism, not sizing.",
        "priority": "high",
        "status": "done",
        "owner": "",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "Only the destination consumes detail",
          "Repeated activation of the same graph is geometrically idempotent",
          "Right-click opens its menu without centering or triggering expansion; explicit menu focus remains separate"
        ],
        "definitionKey": "task",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "task",
