      "data": {
        "title": "Lay out around expanded and compact frames",
        "body": "Update layoutWorkspaceInstances and placement helpers to use focus-dependent frames. Settle automatic neighbors around the focused document; resolve Q3 for manually positioned/pinned neighbors. Preserve graph-local content and stable identities.\n\nStarted 2026-09-25, resolving Q3 first: placementFootprint() now governs both nextRegionOffset() and reflowWorkspaceInstances(), reserving each instance's authored/expansion-plan size (not its current draw size) from its neighbors, with the existing minimum gap. 6 new tests in graphWorkspace.test.js proving a compact neighbor still reserves its authored footprint, a newly placed graph clears that reserved footprint (not just the neighbor's compact box), and settling draws each neighbor at its own current size while still planning around footprints. Full suite 1083/1083. Remaining: layoutWorkspaceInstances() still has to actually choose compact vs authored per focus (this only made the room for that choice safe to make); the goal text's \"neighboring graphs settle around the changed frames\" should be read as the corrective, rare case now, not the routine one.",
        "priority": "high",
        "status": "in-progress",
        "owner": "",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "No overlap among automatically placed frames after settling",
          "Alternating focus settles deterministically without cumulative drift",
          "Zoom changes represented View selection but never invokes frame/layout transitions"
        ],
