      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "body": "Recommendation: keep pinned/manual positions fixed and move automatic neighbors; when constraints conflict, use an explicit bounded policy rather than silently rewriting manual placement. Decide whether any overlap is acceptable in constrained layouts.\n\nRESOLVED (2026-09-25), and reframed by the owner: expansion should not be a traumatic event for the layout at all, pinned or not. Built: placementFootprint() -- every instance reserves its authored (potentially-focused) size from its neighbors, never its current compact or transient draw size, plus the existing 120-unit minimum gap. nextRegionOffset() (new-graph placement) and reflowWorkspaceInstances() (live settling) both plan around this now, so a graph drawn small still keeps the room its own expansion plan needs. In the common case this means focusing something later needs to displace nobody, pinned or automatic, because the distance was already reserved when things were placed. manuallyPlaced still distinguishes what the live settle pass may reposition -- that is a separate concern (whether the system may move something at all) from whether expansion is disruptive when it does.",
        "status": "resolved",
        "owner": "",
        "resolutionPath": "components/GraphEditor/utils/graphWorkspace.js",
        "prominence": "high",
